A||||9||Fformula88||Televisions... your recomendations||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||12-27-2000||05:58 PM||||I am in the market for a new TV and was wondering what everyone's opinions are about these new "flat screen" TV's.  I am on somewhat of a budget and will be getting a 27" TV.  It won't be going into a very big room, and is replacing a 25".  Yesterday I went looking at them and liked a couple models.  JVC has two, their D-series which is a regular tube and their i-scan flat screen.  There is a $300 price jump on the flat screen, but it has a much more advanced digital filter and of course the flat screen.  Both Sony and Phillips/Magnavox have flat screens priced about the same and a hundred less than the JVC.  Picture quality is close between the three.  I can afford any of them, but of course hate to spend any more than I have to.  So is the fancier digitial filter in the JVC worht the added cost over the Sony/Phillips models.  Also, is the flat screen that much of an improvement to warrent its added cost over the regualr tube TV's?  Thanks for all opinions.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||12-27-2000||07:10 PM||||I have the regular JVC 27" you were talking about.  We picked it up for a very reasonable price, and it is working very well.  The picture quality with a DVD player is also very good.  If I had the money for a flat screen, I would go for that though.  They sure are nice.  BUT, you could probably buy a nice 32" for the same price...<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-27-2000||07:36 PM||||did the sony have the s video hook up? i heard at one time they did on their flat screens and no one else did. if so it might be something to consider if you want to get into the multi-media thing in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||12-27-2000||09:26 PM||||Go for Sony.  They make the best TVs and they will last forever.  The new WEGA's have the best picture! I just wish I could afford one!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000004||rodmcneill||12-27-2000||10:12 PM||||The Sony Wega's do have a great picture. I think the 32" Wega will be my next tv.||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||12-27-2000||10:27 PM||||I have a JVC 27" D Series and I love it. It has the 3 line digital comb filter and the side surround speakers. It also has composite & S Video inputs, as well as the front panel inputs (handy if you have a Playstation or console). I love it, watching S-Video quality movies off my Dish the picture is super. I'm pretty sure the model number is 27120 D. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||12-27-2000||10:30 PM||||I forgot to mention that the JVC has a really neat color correction filter called Theatre mode. It adjusts the contrast and the colors, vastly improving the image. Also, the D series tube has edge correction so that the screen seems almost flat. If you want to compare Televisions, go to <A HREF="http://www.futureshop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.futureshop.com</A>  They have a neat little comparison chart where you can compare different models online.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||12-29-2000||11:07 AM||||Sonys are good. I have a 35'' JVC that works great, absolutely no probs. Dont get RCA had nothing but problems and paid $1800 for it. Also just a note on Phillips-Magnavox, there warranty is not worth the paper its printed on at least with experience i had. I love getting new hi tech stuff, but Ill wait for big flat screens to come down, way to high for me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||12-29-2000||05:23 PM||||Roger, sorry to hear your bad luck with Phillips-Magnavox.  I have had very good luck with their equipment.  I was looking at those HDTV's for playing movies and stuff in the widebar format too.  They are $9999.00!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Their piucture is SOOOO good, but I'd have to take out a loan for it!  LOL.  I currently have a GE, which is made by RCA and the board is finished on it.  I've only had it since 96 and am very unimpressed.<P>Right now I am leaning towards getting the Sony WEGA.  I'm going out this evening to look at 'em.  I lkie the JVC, but the Sony is a couple hundred cheaper.  I love new equipment too, but have to buy it before the Fiero hits the road this spring.  It is sure to take the majority of my free money!  hehehe. <P>Thanks for everyone's imput!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fformula88||12-30-2000||04:33 PM||||Again, thanks everyone for all the input.  I decided to get the JVC D-series.  Its an awesome TV with just about all the goodies I could want.  After staring at it next to a Flat screen for a while at a "normal" viewing distance I decided the $200 dollar difference wasn't enough for the flat screen.  Its a neat TV, but I have too many other places to spend that cash.  As it turns out I ended up spending a lot of it on Optical and video caples to hook up all my components (receiver with the TV and DVD).  Its a great TV, and WOW I cannot believe the picture from the DVD's!||||reg||1
